ch are not suited tiles, so not possible.\n\nLower Tiles requires only suited tiles of 1,2,3, no honors.\n\nSimilarly.\n\nPerhaps Mixed Straight or other.\n\nBut with B1 discarded, I have one less terminal.\n\nBut T9 is still there.\n\nAnother pattern: Knitted Straight, but I have W1,W3,W6,W7; T1,T2,T4,T6,T9; not matching the knitted pattern.\n\nKnitted requires specific: e.g., 1,4,7 of one suit, etc.\n\nFor example, if I had B1,B4,B7; T2,T5,T8; W3,W6,W9.\n\nBut I have W1,W3,W6,W7 \u2014 W1 and W7 could be for dots, but not.\n\nNot close.\n\nPerhaps it's better to aim for a hand with chows.\n\nFor example, I can try to form:\n\n- 123 in bamboos: with T1,T2, need T3\n\n- 456 in bamboos: with T4,T6, need T5\n\n- 678 in characters: with W6,W7, need W8\n\n- And a pair or something.\n\nBut I have W1 and W3, which could be 123 with W2.\n\nBut I can't have two 123 in different suits easily.\n\nW1 and W3 for 123, T1 and T2 for 123, but same numbers different suits.\n\nFor Pure Straight, I need 123,456,789 in same suit, which I don't have.\n\nMixed Straight: 123,456,789 in different suits.\n\nFor example, 123 in bamboos, 456 in characters, 789 in dots, but I have no dots except B1 discarded.\n\nAfter discard, no dots.\n\nSo 789 could be in bamboos or characters.\n\nI have T9, so 789 in bamboos possible with T7,T8.\n\nCharacters: W6,W7 for 678 or 567.\n\nW1,W3 for 123.\n\nSo possible Mixed Straight: e.g., 123 in characters (W1,W2,W3), 456 in bamboos (T4,T5,T6), 789 in bamboos but same suit, Mixed Straight requires different suits for each chow.\n\nMixed Straight: three chows of 123, 456, 789 in three different suits.\n\nBut I have only two suits now: characters and bamboos, no dots.\n\nSo I can't have three different suits; I have only two suits.\n\nTherefore, Mixed Straight is impossible after discarding B1.\n\nSimilarly, Pure Straight requires one suit.\n\nBut I have two suits, so not pure.\n\nWith two suits, possible patterns: Half Flush, which is one suit and honors.\n\nHalf Flush is worth 6 points.\n\nFor example, if I can have all characters and honors, or all bamboos and honors.\n\nCurrently, I have four characters, five bamboos, four honors.\n\nIf I discard bamboos, I can go for characters and honors.\n\nBut I have W1,W3,W6,W7 \u2014 not a full suit.\n\nSimilarly for bamboos.\n\nBut it's possible.\n\nHalf Flush is 6 points, which is low, but with other patterns.\n\nFor example, if I have a dragon pung, etc.\n\nBut let's not digress.\n\nBack to discard choice.\n\nPerhaps discarding a bamboo middle tile.\n\nAnother idea: the previous player discarded T8, so T8 is out, which might make T7 and T9 safer or less safe, but T9 might be wanted for 789.\n\nBut since T8 is discarded, players might be less likely to have 789, so T9 could be safer to discard.\n\nSimilarly, in some cases, discarding terminals early is good.\n\nBut for me, T9 is the only high terminal I have.\n\nI also have W7, which is high character.\n\nW7 is 7, not terminal; terminal is 1 or 9.\n\nW7 is middle-high.\n\nTerminals are 1 and 9.\n\nSo W7 is not terminal.\n\nOnly W1, T1, T9, B1 are terminals.\n\nAfter discarding B1, terminals are W1, T1, T9.\n\nT9 is terminal.\n\nIf I discard T9, I lose that terminal.\n\nBut for patterns, it might be ok.\n\nI think B1 is still a good choice.\n\nLet's see what the valid actions suggest.\n\nPerhaps I can look for tiles that are not needed for common hands.\n\nAnother pattern: since I have many 1s, but different suits.\n\nFor example, Triple Pung of 1s, but different suits, not possible; pung must be same suit or honor.\n\nPung is three identical tiles, so for numbers, same suit.\n\nSo W1, T1, B1 are different, so not a pung.\n\nSimilarly.\n\nSo no.\n\nI think I should discard B1.\n\nMoreover, in the answer choices, Play B1 is listed.\n\nNow, to confirm, let's see if there's a better discard.\n\nWhat about T4? T4 is 4, which is even, but not particularly special.\n\nOr W3, but I have W1 and W3.\n\nDiscarding W3 might be bad because